From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_pm8226_bms: do not wake for polling

This BMS has no wake IRQ. Its periodic freezable work reports battery
properties through power_supply_changed(), which otherwise activates a
wakeup source and can abort suspend during filesystem sync. Suppress that
software wake source; charger, power-key and RTC wake sources are separate.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pm8226_bms.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pm8226_bms.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pm8226_bms.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pm8226_bms.c
@@ -364,5 +364,7 @@ static int pm8226_bms_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return -ERANGE;
 
+	/* Periodic battery polling must not abort system suspend. */
+	cfg.no_wakeup_source = true;
 	cfg.drv_data = bms;
 	cfg.fwnode = dev_fwnode(dev);
 	bms->battery = devm_power_supply_register(dev, &pm8226_bms_desc, &cfg);
